+# Actual Pal Remove in one bounded Host source domain
+
+Feature3 remains partial. This checkpoint executes the original common Pal,
+PeopleTable/NameCard handlers, PSF pager, RootHttpRequest and request serializer
+in an owned Node process with declared Qt/ListModel/pointer/account primitives.
+A real owned two-account HTTPS service receives the normal submissions and
+DELETE. It is not a test Domain, installed Pico application or native publisher.
+No public capability, SourceReady, Native/Qt, isolated Actor or complete-feature
+flag is enabled.
+
+## Actual operation and custody
+
+One fresh normal request/accept establishes the relationship through two actual
+authenticated POSTs. The original pager supplies a current username-bound row.
+The existing TokenAvatarPeopleUI validates the actual Host row and separate
+current NativeBefore-equivalent original before each normal row/Remove input.
+Command, intent and first ACK storage are booked before delivery. The declared
+pointer leaf invokes the original QML handler, which rechecks its own observed
+nonce/fingerprint and original1.5-second clock before unchanged Pal sends the
+real DELETE. A completed reply with matching original URL/API/body/bearer fields
+and response ID joins the current same-account model absence/count/revision.
+The original product's totalEntries may remain historical after row removal;
+model.complete therefore stays false rather than repairing product state.
+
+The external Root witness keeps Reader and Peer credentials outside the adapter.
+It binds the actual original fixture instance before the effect, independently
+GETs normal authenticated absence for each account and joins the actual service
+DELETE receipt. Separate protocol roles in this Host process are not isolated
+Actor processes. No expected-state endpoint or requested relationship row is
+accepted. The default service remains strict Iamus POST/data.connection. The
+explicit legacy profile admits the existing Pico top-level connection envelope
+and read-only GET polling only after a genuine submission; both actual POSTs
+remain necessary for a relationship.
+
+Every acquired HTTP/IPC/Source literal is strong before its postguard and is
+retained in one original AudioRawArchive before framing or JSON decoding.
+Actual pipe capacities and paired original descriptors are queried before
+producer enable. Unknown input/EOF/HTTP/source states retain original pending
+claims and first error contexts without retry, fallback, truncation or eviction.
+Known Node wait, pipe EOF, account/TLS/thread and Host descriptor closure are
+resource facts. The external witness work token and all permanent claims remain
+held through terminal; this is not Native/family clean retirement.
+
+## Additive bounds and default behavior
+
+The canonical Native profile retains Native6MiB plus Host4MiB and its original
+262,144-byte envelope. Its producer and complete normal Common path remain
+unavailable in this checkpoint. The separate declared Node profile books the
+entire existing Node8MiB, Host parser1MiB, copied-file/descriptor/footer256KiB,
+selected-row4KiB, Caller2MiB, pre-count2MiB and metadata512KiB:14,422,016 bytes
+before actual Parent live/file/cache, Raw/index/parts, pending literal/side
+claims and the unchanged three64KiB proof windows. The declared parser checks
+65,536 actual bytes and4,096 lexical tokens before JSON, including escaped
+quotes; it does not weaken the Native default grammar or envelope. The original
+16MiB/512/HTTP16/input20s/Source1.5s/owning120s fences stay unchanged. Admission
+must prove the actual prospective sum, rather than infer that every scope fits.
+
+A fixed original producer owns the same bank/guard/bill throughout. All work
+and future descriptor slots are booked before fixture construction. The shared
+attachment binds the original Family pointer once and checks it before bill
+delegation. There is no unknown archive adoption or Native budget setter.
+`people2=None` preserves legacy Parent1/2/3 behavior. Parent4 is a private Source2
+context grammar and must not be adopted by the old route. The Source2 private
+capture/input protocols do not enable normal Common operations. Optional QML
+observation hooks stay unavailable when their Native producer is absent.
+
+## Evidence and remaining work
+
+The private first coherent component passed7.465s (9.168s outer), with15,202
+source files unchanged,20 original output files checked twice by SHA/stat8,
+no children and four known Host resource-close results. Actual data show2POST,
+1DELETE,2 normal pointer boundaries,6 Source captures and both authenticated
+absence GETs. The pre-close bill was14,904,240 bytes including pending work and
+proof windows. After actual closure the same bank held178 original literals and
+one known permanent work reservation (179 issued reservations). The actual
+Source model changed count1/revision19→20 to count0/revision23; model.complete
+remained false. Older import and final-validator failures remain separate RED
+epochs. These are Host component results, not new repository-test results.
+
+The full coherent Native6 afterimages remain separate. Actual original-header
+object/header/sizeof checks qualified only the available Qt5.15.13 Host subset.
+Project5.15.18/Android, full AccountManager/XMLHttpRequest and TSI linkage remain
+unqualified; actual missing TBB/generated Shader dependencies are not replaced
+with providers or stubs. No partial C++ header hunks are included here that would
+break the existing real native UI link harness. Source builds are authorized;
+missing dependencies and actual linkage still need completion separately.
+
+Next is the same-domain full Cancel/Reject/Accept/Remove and failure/recovery/
+cleanup frontier, followed by the actual Native producer/normal Common join,
+avatar URL/Favorite restoration and final independent lifecycle qualification.
+Earlier separate Phone-derived and Node-only green scopes are not relabeled as
+this whole feature. The fixed Phone5e8 source is read-only and supplies the
+inspected protocol/ownership principles; no Phone files or product envelope are
+repaired by this checkpoint.
